 linked  together  in order to create your ssd so one that  is a downside you cannot upgrade it and  we know that there is enough room inside  of here apple could have added m.2 slots  to allow you to upgrade that or even  just come out now and said hey guys this  is getting blown out of  proportion we will allow you to upgrade  it but you'll have to buy it from us and  have us install it or say hey that will  never happen make sure you purchase the  right amount that you need either way in  a desktop machine it would be nice to  have some upgradeability but at this  point you just need to buy an external  ssd we recommend the new sabrine we made  a whole video about it it's extremely  fast over thunderbolt or usb type c so  if you want to check that out want to  find the best solution how do you make  this yourself and save some money too go  ahead and check out that video after  this one the second one is the fact that  the performance is limited even on the  24 core base model  which does not heat up at all it is  insane now with the macbook pros that  came out we saw that there were some  thermal throttling and limitations due  to these powerful chips being in small  laptops that are battery powered and  have to be cooled down and we saw that  the chip actually slows down to three  gigahertz instead of 3.2 running at full  blast like the m1s do but we figured  that is because of cooling and things  like that and with this machine having  this amazing cooler they would actually  allow you to use the full performance  and no we found that no matter what we  did  this two thousand dollar model actually  ran slightly slower in certain tests  than a macbook pro on battery power it  still had the same limitations running  at three gigahertz at full blast and in  some cases where uh the system would  throttle down for example the graphics  wouldn't run at full 1300 it'd run at  about 1250 or so  we still had that same slowdown in this  machine even though the gpu was running  at like 61 degrees celsius full blast  and the cpu at 71 that's after an  extended test that's maxing everything  out it pretty much shows that this chip  is limited exactly like the macbooks are  there's a profile set for power usage  and different things like that that's  not limited by thermal performance or  fan noise or battery anything else  that's just how apple programmed it so  they could have gave us more performance  in the system  higher frequencies no limitations but  they didn't so either they want the  performance to be the same across from  the laptops or the desktops or they're  just keeping it capped so that when the  m2 comes out that will have a much  bigger boost both in terms of different  architecture and improvements and core  counts and actually being able to clock  up higher in frequency which they  definitely plan for as far as wattage  and thermals now the third one is the m1  ultra on stage they showed off this  beautiful huge new chip and said that  because of their interconnect with the  crazy high bandwidth the system sees  this as one chip instead of two  different graphics modules like sli for  example with nvidia and so you get the  full performance without any bottlenecks  well with our testing we see that we're  not getting proper scaling and even  worse if you're buying an m1 ultra and  you're spending the extra to get the  full 64 cores that they showed off on  stage which is a thousand bucks that  actually has about 33 percent more  graphics cores compared to the 48 core  model so you think you get extra  performance especially in benchmarks  right well in gfx bench metal which is  very well optimized we are only seeing a  16  increase in performance instead of 33  more cores  and in 3d marks wildlife which is also  optimized we're seeing a difference of  20 and that is just gpu limited so the  scaling is not perfect now to prove this  in our craziest test the highest wattage  we saw used was 87 watts and on stage  apple showed up a graph saying it's  capable of  105 watts and then with that if we take  these same graphics course and we look  at the m1 that only has eight that  actually runs at 15 watts so when you  scale all the way up to 64 you should be  getting  120 watts total to get the peak  performance but we are only seeing 87  which is why the performance is also not  scaling very well so there's definitely  something going on and we know that  thermal limitations aren't there it's  running super cool insanely cool like i  said 61 degrees celsius when we were  just hitting it super hard for an  extended amount of time and the fan was  at idle which is insane so the scaling  isn't working out as well as apple kind  of talked about now with that with that  we also are making that triple  comparison to actually show you the  increase in performance for real world  tasks not just benchmarks and how much  more performance you can expect if  you're spending the extra for them on  ultra or especially the extra thousand  bucks for the full unlocked one so if  you guys want to see that make sure your  notifications are enabled now the next  one we have to talk about is software  and this is a huge disappointment for me  software sees that the same chip that  they had before just more cores  but we are not getting the great best  performance overall we are doing our  benchmark tests right now and what we  see is that final cut it hasn't been  updated for four months now and all the  tests that apple showed on stage as far  as final cut and the performance of it  it was using pre-release software  whereas right now they have not given us  those they gave it to the reviewers that  apple sent the machines to but not to  the public so right now this system is  still locked down it's been over a week  and we don't have the software that can  fully utilize it so some software is  being updated but one of what i want to  let you guys know of is that just  because you're buying the best 