mance but we also have done a  ton of testing and we show that 32 gigs  of ram performs identical to 64 in  almost all the cases even when you're  running parallels and you're running  windows you're running games and  benchmarks in windows and mac at the  same time you're just throwing  everything you can with tons of tabs  insanity with your system the difference  is almost not there because the unified  memory architect architecture is just so  insanely efficient and fast and the ssds  are fast so having to spend the extra  money just to go for the ultra makes it  such a big jump that makes it kind of  tough now i wish that you could still  get 32 gigs with the m1 ultra make it a  lot more affordable now we know that  apple they're good at making you spend  money the ram upgrades are expensive if  it's built into the motherboard it's  expensive but now they have another step  up on how to get you to spend more money  because you don't have the option  anymore to have a lower amount of ram if  your program doesn't need it but more  graphics performance on the other hand  if you do need more graphics performance  so that is a bummer and that leads me  into the price tag of these things now  for two grand you're getting a great  deal at the base price point the m1 max  the 24 core you have enough ram ssd it's  a killer deal but it's such a big jump  from the mac mini whereas for a lot of  people they cannot justify it so it  would be nice to have something in  between maybe with the m1 pro at the  middle price tag now we know that  apple's working on something like this  they are gonna address that need we're  not sure exactly when hopefully soon but  that will probably have the m2 chip  which is going to have faster single  core performance and better efficiency  and maybe maybe better scalability as  well so if you're having a hard time  spending that 2 grand  or even more so if you want to do  upgrades i would say just hold off a bit  wait on buying one of these 